<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rory O'Donnell, 1st Earl of Tyrconnell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1575">1575</a>–<a href="/years/1608">1608</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rory O'Donnell was the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-hugh-odonnell">Red Hugh O'Donnell</a> and succeeded him as chief of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">Tír Chonaill</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a> he submitted to the English crown and was made Earl of Tyrconnell in 1603. Fearing arrest, he left Ireland with Hugh O'Neill in the Flight of the Earls in 1607 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> the next year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rory-odonnell-1st-earl-of-tyrconnell.jpg" alt="Rory O'Donnell, 1st Earl of Tyrconnell" width="305" height="500" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Battista Ricci (1537-1627). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rory_O%27Donnell,_Earl_of_Tyrconnell.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
